'''Greeata Jendowanian''' was a [[Gender|female]] [[Rodian]] who worked as a singer and dancer for the [[Max Rebo Band]].<ref name="Music" />

==Biography==
[[File:Faytonni.jpg|thumb|left|150px|Greeata present at the [[Galaxies Opera House]], in the background, center.]]
In [[19 BBY]], towards the end of the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], she attended a performance of a [[Mon Calamari]] opera on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]].<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref> [[4 ABY|Four]] [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Yavin]], she and the rest of the [[Maximilian Rebo|Max Rebo]] Band performed for [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]] at his [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]] on the planet [[Tatooine]]. The group played the song "[[Jedi Rocks]]" for the Hutt, who demanded that they repeat the performance, but then dropped his [[Slavery|slave]] dancer [[Oola]] into his [[rancor]] pit during the performance, causing the band to stop playing leaving them both shocked and annoyed. Greeata was visibly shocked when Oola was eaten by the rancor, and then witnessed [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] arrive in the palace disguised as the [[bounty hunter]] [[Boushh]] with the [[Wookiee]] [[Chewbacca]] as a prisoner.<ref name="RTOJ" /> While on Tatooine, she wore an [[Color|orange]] crest and [[gold]] jewelry.<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref>

Jendowanian and her other members of her band were impressed that [[Jedi Knight]] [[Luke Skywalker]] killed [[Pateesa|Jabba's rancor]]. She fantasied that he had done it to avenge fellow Twi'lek dancer [[Oola]] for being fed to the beast by Jabba.<ref name="Max Rebo 1">[[Return of the Jedi – Max Rebo 1|''Return of the Jedi – Max Rebo'' 1]]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Greeata Jendowanian first appeared in the [[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|Special Edition]] re-release of [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']] in [[1997]], played by [[Celia Fushille-Burke]].<ref name="RTOJ" /> She was first named in the ''[[Star Wars Legends]]'' ''Power of the Force'' set of [[Hasbro]]'s action figure collection which was released in [[1998]].<ref name="PotF">[[Star Wars: The Power of the Force (1995 toy line)|''Star Wars: The Power of the Force'' toy line (1995)]]</ref> The name was confirmed to be [[canon]] by ''[[Music in the Star Wars Galaxy: The Modal Nodes vs. The Max Rebo Band]]'', a [[StarWars.com]] article written by [[Amy Ratcliffe]] and published in [[2015]].<ref name="Music" />

